{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Decision: ADDED the leg (snapshot-gc-worker). Both design questions resolved: (1) staleness IS the shared table — gc_trigger acquires via rebar._store.stamped_lock.stamped_file_lock, which writes the v2 stamp and adjudicates via lock_owner.stamped_file_is_stale, so doctor's _existence_report is the right reader unchanged; (2) root derivation made READ-ONLY via new repo_snapshot.peek_store_root() + gc_trigger.worker_lock_probe_path() (store_root/_gc_dir mkdir as side effects; a diagnostic must not materialise an absent store — it reports the lock free). Doctor tests gain an autouse REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR pin because this is the census's one host-global probe. Pushed as Gerrit change 2099 (commit 3737dbd57a)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787389905760091001,"uuid":"cfb3cfe1-07bd-454b-b40d-fdaf6aff92a5"}